WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.640
Mark Carney and the global order.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:04.397
Goldman Sachs.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:06.160
Bank of Canada.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.910
Bank of England.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.068
United Nations Special Envoy for Climate Action and Finance.

00:00:12.068 --> 00:00:14.625
Brookfield Asset Management.

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:18.102
Chair of the Glasgow Financial Alliance for Net Zero.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:20.909
World Economic Forum board member.

00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:23.534
And now, Prime Minister of Canada.

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:36.818
This page documents one career path and asks one question: when the Prime Minister's professional network is entirely composed of global financial institutions, central banks, and supranational organisations, whose interests does the government serve?

00:00:36.818 --> 00:00:42.511
Every connection documented here is from official records, published appointments, and public filings.

00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:44.272
The career path.

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:49.454
Mark Carney's career moves through the institutions that control global financial architecture.

00:00:49.454 --> 00:00:53.852
Thirteen years at Goldman Sachs, where he rose to Managing Director.

00:00:53.852 --> 00:01:00.965
Then Governor of the Bank of Canada from 2008 to 2013, where he navigated the global financial crisis.

00:01:00.965 --> 00:01:09.784
Then Governor of the Bank of England from 2013 to 2020, the first non-British citizen to hold the role since the Bank's founding in 1694.

00:01:09.784 --> 00:01:13.738
Then UN Special Envoy for Climate Action and Finance.

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:18.579
Then Vice Chairman and Chair of Impact Investing at Brookfield Asset Management.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:21.034
Then Prime Minister of Canada.

00:01:21.034 --> 00:01:23.374
Each role connects to the next.

00:01:23.374 --> 00:01:26.204
Each institution connects to the others.

00:01:26.204 --> 00:01:30.159
World Economic Forum and global institutional connections.

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:38.034
Mark Carney has participated in multiple WEF Annual Meetings at Davos as both a central banker and as a private sector executive.

00:01:38.034 --> 00:01:43.568
He has served on the WEF Board of Trustees — the same board that included Chrystia Freeland.

00:01:43.568 --> 00:01:50.170
The Global Financial Alliance for Net Zero, which Carney created, operates through the WEF's partner network.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:02:03.545
His wife, Diana Fox Carney, has been a senior advisor at the International Institute for Sustainable Development and has been involved in global policy forums on sustainability and the relationship between economic systems and environmental outcomes.

00:02:03.545 --> 00:02:05.715
The conflict architecture.

00:02:05.715 --> 00:02:08.477
The documented conflicts of interest.

00:02:08.477 --> 00:02:13.272
Mark Carney created the global financial framework for climate transition investing.

00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:18.636
He then joined Brookfield Asset Management, which profits from climate transition investments.

00:02:18.636 --> 00:02:24.829
He then became Prime Minister of Canada, which sets the policy environment that determines which investments succeed.

00:02:24.829 --> 00:02:32.159
The same person who designed the global rules, invested under those rules, and now sets the national policy that enforces those rules.

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:38.124
At each stage, the financial interests of the previous role benefit from the policy decisions of the next role.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.522
This is not alleged corruption.

00:02:40.522 --> 00:02:43.624
It is documented institutional architecture.

00:02:43.624 --> 00:02:46.022
The question this page asks.

00:02:46.022 --> 00:03:03.602
When the Prime Minister of Canada spent his career at Goldman Sachs, ran two central banks, chaired the global financial regulatory body, served as UN Special Envoy, served on the WEF Board of Trustees, and led transition investing at a nine-hundred-and-twenty-five-billion-dollar asset manager — whose interests does the government serve?

00:03:03.602 --> 00:03:06.238
This is not about left or right.

00:03:06.238 --> 00:03:12.056
It is about whether elected government serves the people who elected it or the institutions that produced its leader.

00:03:12.056 --> 00:03:16.749
The career path documented on this page is verifiable from official records.

00:03:16.749 --> 00:03:20.443
The question of whose interests it serves is left to the reader.
